{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review gate cleared for the three claimable leaves. 1ecf (D) PASS first time. 06ae (C) BLOCKed twice on E4 divergent-implementation: the plan assumed a per-tool non-deferral lever and contradicted AGENTS.md:173; description rewritten around verified ground truth (ENABLE_TOOL_SEARCH is the ONLY, all-or-nothing lever; .claude/ is gitignored; settings resolve to the main checkout) with corrected AC -> PASS. 84c7 (B) BLOCKed twice: (i) code-review moves ARE already overlay-driven via code_review/moves.py::load_move_registry reading .rebar/code_review_moves.json, so the contingent engine-work scope item is dropped; (ii) a project.* criterion id can never enter code-review's closed {OVERLAY_IDS + always} applies_when vocabulary, so a code-review move keyed on it would be permanently dead -> criterion routed to plan_review ONLY; (iii) blocking_enabled is a code-review-only field that plan-review's threshold_for (criteria/model.py:73-85) never reads, so it was dropped as inert -> PASS. 4143 (A) intentionally NOT reviewed yet: it is blocked by 1ecf, so review-plan would fast-fail; it will be reviewed after D closes, per the dependency-order rule."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785373702892403001,"uuid":"2eda97d6-a82f-48f3-8af2-679e0296a541"}